  'Capnography' => 'Continuous measurement and waveform display of exhaled carbon dioxide, used to assess ventilation, confirm airway placement, and monitor anesthesia, sedation, or critical illness.',
  'Capsular Contracture' => 'Abnormal tightening and hardening of scar tissue around an implant, especially a breast implant, causing firmness, pain, distortion, or displacement.',
  'Capsule Endoscopy' => 'A swallowed camera capsule that photographs the gastrointestinal tract, particularly the small intestine, while passing naturally through the bowel.',
  'Capsule of Glisson' => 'The connective-tissue sheath surrounding the liver and extending with portal tracts around branches of the portal vein, hepatic artery, and bile ducts.',
  'Capsule of Tenon' => 'A fascial sheath surrounding the eyeball and separating it from orbital fat, allowing the globe and extraocular muscles to move smoothly.',
